// Establishes `BasicSummon` as a real player-cast companion, distinct from
// this variant's only other player-spell precedent so far. Every
// already-shipped `BasicSummon` player spell
// (illusion/{minor_illusion_image,silent_image,major_image,project_image}.ron,
// transmutation/floating_disk.ron) is a `with_agent: false`,
// `incorporeal: true`, `phantom_illusion: true`, `has_health: false`
// decorative phantasm or a scripted prop -- none is an actual fighting/
// following creature with its own agency. This spell instead uses the OTHER
// already-real `SummonInfo::Npc` recipe: the one NPC-cast summon abilities
// already use for genuine owned companions (see
// assets/common/abilities/custom/dwarves/forgemaster/summon_iron_dwarf.ron
// and assets/common/abilities/vampire/bloodmoon_heiress/summon.ron) --
// `alignment`/`with_agent`/`incorporeal`/`phantom_illusion`/
// `delete_after_expiry` all left at their `#[serde(default)]` values:
// `alignment: None` resolves to `Alignment::Owned(caster)`, `with_agent`
// defaults to true (it acts on its own AI, matching "obeys your commands"),
// `incorporeal`/`phantom_illusion` default to false (a real, hittable
// creature, not a decoy), and `duration: None` means no expiry timer WITHIN
// this ability's own lifecycle.
//
// KNOWN GAP, reviewed and left open deliberately (content-only pass, no
// Rust touched): `Alignment::Owned` alone does NOT grant the persistence a
// "permanent companion" implies. The real cross-session pet system
// (`comp::Pet`, populated only via `server::pet::tame_pet_internal`, the
// interact-to-tame flow) is what gets saved to the DB on logout
// (`server/src/events/player.rs`'s persistence loop explicitly skips
// `Alignment::Owned` entities without a `Pet` component) and gets an
// `Anchor` to survive its owner's chunk unloading while they're online.
// `BasicSummon`'s `CreateNpcEvent` path never populates `comp::Pet`, so this
// familiar will NOT survive a logout/server-restart, and isn't chunk-unload
// -protected either. Recasting doesn't despawn/replace a prior familiar
// (no cap exists on this summon path, unlike the DB-backed pet system's
// `MAX_PETS`), so repeated casts stack multiple foxes rather than replacing
// one. True permanence/replace-on-recast needs a Lane B follow-up wiring
// `BasicSummon`-created `Alignment::Owned` NPCs through the same
// `comp::Pet`/persistence/anchor path real tamed pets use. This RON still
// establishes the intended CharacterAbility/SummonInfo shape (agent,
// health, ownership) for that follow-up to build on; only the
// cross-session persistence guarantee is currently absent, and neither the
// i18n flavor text nor this comment should overclaim it in the meantime.
//
// `body`: `QuadrupedSmall(Fox)` stands in for "a small animal of your
// choosing" -- no in-cast body-selection UI exists, so one representative
// small-animal body is picked rather than exposing a choice the engine
// can't offer yet.
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 1.0,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 1,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 2.0),
        body: QuadrupedSmall((species: Fox, body_type: Female)),
        scale: None,
        has_health: true,
        use_npc_name: true,
        loadout_config: None,
        skillset_config: None,
        duration: None,
    ),
)
